      "thinking": "My turn 4. I have 3 untapped lands (2 Forest, 1 Plains) plus Raucous Audience can tap for G (it's not sick? It entered turn 3, so it's fine now). So I have effectively 4 mana.\n\
\n\
Options: Earth Kingdom General {3}{G} — 4 mana, earthbend 2. But wait, Audience taps for GG if I control power 4+ creature — I don't yet. So 3 lands + Audience = 4 mana, can cast General.\n\
\n\
Alternatively Earth Kingdom Jailer {2}{W} — exile Azula (4/3) or Warden. Azula is a big threat with Firebender Ascension quest at 3. Actually exiling Azula removes their biggest threat. Or exile the Ascension (enchantment, MV 2 — no, must be MV 3 or greater).\n\
\n\
Plan: play Jailer exiling Azula now, then later General. Or play General first for earthbend 2 and life gain synergy.\n\
\n\
Jailer exiling Azula: Azula is 4/3 firebending 2 — each attack gives RR and clue. Big threat. Removing it seems great. But also Warden menace pings.\n\
\n\
I have 4 mana: could cast Jailer (3) + nothing else useful (Rocky Rebuke needs target; could use Rebuke with Jailer 3/3 to kill Warden? Jailer just entered, no summoning sickness matters for dealing damage via Rebuke? Rocky Rebuke: target creature you control deals damage — doesn't require tap, summoning sickness doesn't matter for fight effects. So Jailer (3 power) deals 3 to Warden (2/3) — kills it, and Warden deals... no, only my creature deals damage, not both. Rocky Rebuke is one-sided \"deals damage equal to its power\" — actually it says \"Target creature you control deals damage equal to its power to target creature an opponent controls.\" One-sided. So Jailer kills Warden, takes nothing.\n\
\n\
That's huge: Jailer exiles Azula, Rebuke kills Warden. Mana: Jailer {2}{W} + Rebuke {1}{G} = 5 mana. I have 3 lands + Audience = 4. Not enough.\n\
\n\
Alternative: Audience {1}{G} + ... hmm. Another Raucous Audience triggers Haru earthbend.\n\
\n\
Option A: Cast General (4 mana), earthbend 2. Then next turn more mana.\n\
Option B: Cast Jailer exiling Azula (3 mana), keep Rebuke for later. Leaves Warden alive which menaces + pings.\n\
Option C: Audience + Rebuke: cast Audience {1}{G} (earthbend 1 from Haru), then Rebuke with Audience... power 2, not enough for Warden (3 toughness). Use Haru? 1. Land creature? earthbent land is 1/1 (from Audience trigger). Could Rebuke with the land creature: 1 damage. Not enough.\n\
\n\
Actually with General: earthbend 2 makes a land 2/2 with haste. Rebuke with that deals 2 — not enough for Warden, but kills Soldier token. Meh.\n\
\n\
Better: Jailer exiling Azula is premium removal. Warden remains but it's 2/3. Their Ascension has 3 quest counters — Azula attacking would trigger copy (4+ counters). Removing Azula neuters the Ascension mostly (only token firebending triggers remain... actually Warden has firebending 1 too, so attacks still add counters).\n\
\n\
Azula is the biggest threat. Cast Jailer now, exile Azula. Then next turn with 5 mana (draw land hopefully + General + maybe Audience).\n\
\n\
Wait, also should I cast Raucous Audience first {1}{G} to trigger Haru earthbend, then Jailer? Total 4 mana = 3 lands + Audience tap. Order: play nothing — land drop: I have no land in hand? Hand: Allies at Last, Avatar's Wrath, General, Jailer, Audience, Rebuke. No land. So 4 mana total.\n\
\n\
Cast Audience ({1}{G}) → Haru earthbend 1 (make a land 1/1 haste). Then cast Jailer ({2}{W}) exiling Azula. Mana: 1+3=4, uses 2 Forest, Plains, and... wait Audience needs G, Jailer needs 2W. Lands: Forest, Forest, Plains + old Audience taps G. So G from new? No—new Audience is summoning sick, can't tap. Sources: F, F, P, old Audience (G). Pay Audience new: G (forest). Jailer: 2W = Plains + forest + ... {2}{W} = two generic + white: Plains for W, forest + old Audience for 2 generic. Total: 2 Forests + Plains + old Audience = 4 mana. Works.\n\
\n\
That gives me: extra 1/1 land creature, board of Haru, 2 Audiences, Jailer, exiled Azula. Next turn maybe General with earthbend.\n\
\n\
Seems strong. Let's do it: cast Raucous Audience first.",
