Mana available: 3 lands + 2 Audiences = 5 mana (GGG... colors: Forest, Forest, Plains + G + G). Jailer {2}{W} and General {3}{G} = 7 total, too much. Can't cast both this turn.\n\
\n\
Which first? Jailer exiles Warden — removes their only creature. Ascension has 4 counters but without creatures attacking it's inert. Opponent has 2 cards in hand. If I cast General first, Warden keeps hitting me (menace 2/3 + token? token is gone? board shows no Soldier token — just Warden. Wait, token gone too — they used Deadly Precision on Haru? Deadly Precision in gy. Token must have attacked and... maybe I blocked? No. Hmm, token not on board — maybe opponent sacrificed token to Deadly Precision as additional cost (sacrifice a creature). Yes! Deadly Precision: pay {4} or sacrifice artifact/creature. They sacrificed the token to kill Haru. That makes sense.\n\
\n\
So opponent has only Warden. I'm at 11. Jailer on Warden clears their board — then they need to draw creatures for Ascension. I think Jailer is the play this turn. Also cast... with 5 mana (FFP + G + G), Jailer costs 2W (Plains + 2). Then remaining 2 mana (Forest + Audience G) — not enough for General (3G). Rocky Rebuke for 1G could kill... nothing to target after Jailer exiles Warden.\n\
\n\
Also play Plains land. So: play Plains, cast Jailer exiling Warden. Next turn General.\n\
\n\
Actually wait — could I cast General first (earthbend 2, gain life when counters put), then attack? No, Warden menace still threatens. Jailer first.\n\
\n\
