      "reasoning": "I'm at 13 with a strong board (General, Jailer, earthbent Forest, two Audiences) versus their Trebuchet, Treetop Freedom Fighters, and token. Time to leverage my advantage — I'll play my Plains, then use Rocky Rebuke to clear their hasty 2/1 before swinging in.",
      "thinking": "Let me analyze the board. I'm at 13hp, opponent at 12hp.\n\
\n\
My board: Earth Kingdom General 2/2, Earth Kingdom Jailer 3/3, Forest (2/2 earthbent, can attack), 2 Forests, 2 Plains, two Raucous Audiences 2/1.\n\
\n\
Opponent board: Ally Token 1/1 (sick), Trebuchet 0/4 defender, Firebender Ascension (4 quest counters), Treetop Freedom Fighters 2/1. Wait — they played Treetop Freedom Fighters? That's a white card... they have Swamps and Mountains only. Interesting — the Ally token and Treetop must be... Hmm, Treetop Freedom Fighters is {1}{R}? Actually the reference shows \"Treetop Freedom Fighters 2/1: Haste, When ETB create a 1/1 white Ally token.\" It's likely a red card. OK.\n\
\n\
So opponent's turn 6: they played Treetop Freedom Fighters (haste 2/1) + token? Wait, the recap said they played Fire Navy Trebuchet on turn 6. Now it's turn 7, my turn — the board shows they have Treetop Freedom Fighters 2/1 too. So on their turn 7 they must have played Treetop Freedom Fighters and attacked with it + Boulder token? Wait, my hp is 13 — was 13 at end of my turn 6. They didn't attack with anything? Trebuchet's trigger creates a 2/1 flying attacking Boulder when they attack. If they attacked with Treetop Freedom Fighters (2/1 haste) they'd create a Boulder too, dealing 4 potentially. I'm at 13, same as before. Maybe they didn't attack? Or maybe they attacked and I blocked? No — it's my turn 7 now, I had no blockers decision apparently. Hmm, maybe they just played Treetop Freedom Fighters without attacking, since attacking would trigger Ascension? Whatever — log details.\n\
\n\
Actually the Trebuchet trigger fires \"whenever you attack\" — they could attack with just the token or just Treetop. If they attacked with Treetop 2/1 + Boulder 2/1 flying = 4 damage, I'd be at 9. I'm at 13, so they didn't attack. Perhaps they played Treetop and held back. Or maybe the log shows something. Let me check the game log for details.\n\
\n\
My turn 7: I have 5 lands (3 Forests, 2 Plains) — one Forest is a 2/2 creature (still a land). Plus 2 Raucous Audiences that tap for G each (GG if I control power-4 creature — no, my biggest is 3/3 Jailer). So mana: 5 lands + 2 dorks = 7 mana.\n\
\n\
Hand: Avatar's Wrath {2}{WW}, Plains, Rocky Rebuke {1}{G}.\n\
\n\
Opponent at 12hp. My attackers: General 2/2, Jailer 3/3, earthbent Forest 2/2, two Audiences 2/1 each = 11 power total. Their blockers: Trebuchet 0/4 (defender — can't block? No wait, defender means it can't attack, but it CAN block. Defender only prevents attacking!). Hmm — important correction: defender creatures can block. Trebuchet 0/4 reach can block. Treetop Freedom Fighters 2/1 can block, Ally token 1/1 (summoning sick — can't block? No, summoning sickness only prevents attacking and tap abilities, blocking is fine... actually summoning sick creatures CAN block). Wait — \"Ally Token 1/1 (sick, token)\" — sick creatures can still block.\n\
\n\
So blockers: 0/4, 2/1, 1/1. My attackers: 2/2, 3/3, 2/2, 2/1, 2/1 = 11 power. If I swing all: they block 3 creatures. Best case for them: block Jailer 3/3 with 0/4 (Jailer dies? 3 damage to Trebuchet, Trebuchet 0/4 survives, Jailer takes 0 — Jailer lives). Block General 2/2 with Treetop 2/1 (both die). Block Forest 2/2 with 1/1 (token dies, Forest survives... 1 damage to 2/2). Then two Audiences 2/1 get through = 4 damage → opponent at 8.\n\
\n\
Alternatively, I have Rocky Rebuke: target creature I control deals damage equal to power to target creature opponent controls. Could use Jailer 3/3 to kill Treetop Freedom Fighters precombat. Then attackers get through more.\n\
\n\
Or Avatar's Wrath: airbend all creatures except up to one. Airbend = exile and return? Actually airbend: \"exile target creature, its controller may cast it... \" hmm. Avatar's Wrath: \"Choose up to one target creature, then airbend all other creatures. Until your next turn, opponents can't cast spells from anywhere other than their hand.\" Airbend presumably exiles a creature and its controller can pay... Let me recall Avatar set mechanics: airbend = exile it, and its owner may cast it from exile for {2} less? Something like \"exile it. Until it...\" Actually in the Avatar set, airbend: \"Exile it. For as long as it remains exiled, its owner may cast it for {2} less.\" I think airbend gives the owner ability to cast from exile by paying its cost minus 2. Let me get oracle text for \"airbend\" — it's a keyword. The card reference partially describes it.\n\
\n\
If I cast Avatar's Wrath keeping my Jailer, all my other creatures (General, Audiences, earthbent Forest — the Forest is a land creature!) get airbent too. Airbending a land? The earthbent Forest would be exiled and return to battlefield tapped (earthbend: \"When it dies or is exiled, return it to the battlefield tapped\"). So it comes back tapped. My Audiences and General would be exiled, and I could recast them for {2} less? That costs tempo but gains value.\n\
\n\
Not great. Avatar's Wrath is best as a defensive reset. I'm ahead on board — I don't want to wrath my own board.\n\
\n\
Plan: Use Rocky Rebuke with Jailer (3/3) to kill Trebuchet (0/4)? 3 damage doesn't kill 0/4. Kill Treetop Freedom Fighters (2/1) — yes, Jailer deals 3 to it. Or use General... Rocky Rebuke costs {1}{G}. I have mana.\n\
\n\
Actually better: attack with everything. Let me compute: 11 power vs 3 blockers (0/4, 2/1, 1/1). They can block 3 of 5 attackers. Optimal blocks for them: Trebuchet on Jailer (3/3) — Jailer deals 3 to Trebuchet, survives; Jailer takes 0. Treetop 2/1 blocks General 2/2: both die. Token blocks Forest 2/2: token dies. Two Audiences through for 4. Opponent at 8.\n\
\n\
If I Rocky Rebuke Treetop with Jailer first (Treetop dies), then attack all: blockers are 0/4 and 1/1. They block Jailer with 0/4 and one 2-power thing with token; 7 power gets through (11-3-1... wait). Attackers: 2/2 General, 3/3 Jailer, 2/2 Forest, 2/1, 2/1. Blocked: Jailer (by Trebuchet), one 2/2 (by token). Through: 2/2 + 2/1 + 2/1 = 6 damage → opponent at 6. \n\
\n\
Alternatively, Rocky Rebuke the Trebuchet? 3 damage doesn't kill 0/4. Rocky Rebuke with... General is 2/2 — can't kill anything meaningful. Jailer is my biggest.\n\
\n\
Hmm, but wait — do I want to keep Rebuke for later? Killing Treetop 2/1 gains 2 damage through (they'd block 2/2 with 2/1 trading, now token blocks it and dies). Fine.\n\
\n\
Actually, better idea: attack first, then decide? No — Rebuke is a sorcery-speed? Rocky Rebuke {1}{G} — likely a sorcery? It says cast {1}{G}, type probably Instant. Fight spells usually instant/sorcery. Let me just check: if instant, I could use it in combat. But it targets \"target creature you control deals damage equal to its power to target creature an opponent controls\" — I could use it post-blocks to kill a blocker. Actually simpler to kill Treetop precombat.\n\
\n\
Also should I play the Plains land drop? I have 5 lands; playing Plains gives 6 + dorks = 8 mana. Hand after: Avatar's Wrath needs {2}{WW} — I have only 2 Plains now, playing a third Plains gives more white. But I'm not casting Wrath this turn (I'm ahead; airbending my own stuff is bad).\n\
\n\
Actually, hold on — what about Avatar's Wrath as an alpha strike? Choose my Jailer, airbend everything else: their Trebuchet, Treetop, token get exiled — they can recast by paying... airbend lets owner cast from exile for its mana cost? Trebuchet owner would need to recast. My other creatures also get airbent. That's a mess — I'd lose my board too. Not an alpha strike since I keep only one creature.\n\
\n\
So: Turn 7 plan — cast Rocky Rebuke (Jailer deals 3 to Treetop Freedom Fighters, killing it), play Plains, then swing with everything. 6 damage through → opponent at 6.\n\
\n\
Wait, actually should I even Rebuke? Consider not using it: they block optimally: 4 through → 8. With Rebuke: 6 through → 6. Rebuke also kills their 2/1 haster. Worth it.\n\
\n\
Mana: Rebuke {1}{G} — tap a Forest. Then attack with General, Jailer, earthbent Forest, both Audiences. Note: Audiences tap for mana — but I don't need more mana after Rebuke... Actually let me play Plains first (land drop), then Rebuke using one Forest, leaving mana open? No other spells worth casting. Avatar's Wrath costs 4 with WW — I could keep it available but I won't cast it.\n\
\n\
Hmm wait, one more consideration: should I hold back blockers? They're at 12, their board: Trebuchet (can't attack), Ascension (4 quest counters — but no creatures with firebending triggers currently except new plays), they have 27 cards in library, ~5-6 cards in hand? Unknown. After I swing, their board: Trebuchet 0/4 (blocks), token 1/1 dead if it blocks. On their turn, Trebuchet can't attack (defender). So no reprisal risk except new haste creatures.\n\
\n\
Swing all. Order: play Plains, cast Rocky Rebuke targeting Jailer and their Treetop Freedom Fighters. Then attack with all 5.\n\
\n\
Wait — one thing: Rocky Rebuke with Jailer — Jailer takes damage equal to Treetop's power (2) since it's a fight-style \"deals damage equal to power to target creature\" — does the other creature deal back? \"Target creature you control deals damage equal to its power to target creature an opponent controls.\" — one-sided, no damage back. Jailer survives regardless.\n\
\n\
Let me also send a chat message (been 2 turns). Then act.\n\
\n\
