\n\
Just attack with all. But wait — opponent might have tricks. Attack all: opponent blocks the biggest (Jailer 3/3), takes 2+2+2=6 damage — exactly lethal. If they have a removal spell on one attacker, still takes... they could kill one unblocked creature; then 2+2=4, not lethal. Consider casting Avatar's Wrath first to airbend Trebuchet? Wrath airbends ALL creatures except up to one target. My board would get bounced too. Hmm, actually \"airbend all other creatures\" — target one creature to keep, everything else gets airbent (exiled, castable for {2}). That resets my board — bad.\n\
\n\
Better: attack all. If they kill one attacker with removal, I take... they block Jailer, kill one 2/2, I deal 4, they're at 2. Then next turn? They have topdeck mode. Alternatively, I can first use Rocky Rebuke to damage Trebuchet? Can't kill.\n\
